 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# NanoCore-S1 Training Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "Auto-runs Stage 1 base training on Kaggle/Colab GPU, commits results back to GitHub.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook eliminates GPU waste by **validating the training pipeline locally first** via `--dry-run`, then launching the full cloud training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 0: Train Tokenizer (32,768 vocab)\n",
    "\n",
    "Trains byte-level BPE tokenizer on FineWeb-EDU data with decision-task special tokens."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train tokenizer (dry-run with sample data first)\n",
    "%time python scripts/train_tokenizer.py --dry-run --output models/tokenizer.json\n",
    "print('\\n--- Dry run complete ---')\n",
    "print('Verifying tokenizer loads and encodes correctly:')\n",
    "from src.tokenizer import NanoCoreTokenizer\n",
    "tok = NanoCoreTokenizer()\n",
    "tok.load('models/tokenizer.json')\n",
    "text = '[STATE] What is the capital of France? [CHOICE] London Paris Berlin Rome [ANSWER] Paris [/ANSWER]'\n",
    "ids = tok.encode(text)\n",
    "decoded = tok.decode(ids)\n",
    "print(f'Vocabulary size: {tok.vocab_size()}')\n",
    "print(f'Encoded ({len(ids)} tokens): {ids[:10]}...')\n",
    "print(f'Decoded: {decoded}')\n",
    "print(f'Special tokens verified: {[tok.ensure_token(t) for t in [\"[STATE]\", \"[CHOICE]\", \"[ANSWER]\", \"[Noul]\"]]}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Full tokenizer training (optional - skips if dry-run output sufficient)\n",
    "# Remove the `--dry-run` flag for production training on FineWeb-EDU\n",
    "\n",
    "import os, json\n",
    "\n",
    "# If dry-run tokenizer exists and you want to skip full training:\n",
    "if not os.path.exists('models/tokenizer.json'):\n",
    "    %time python scripts/train_tokenizer.py --vocab-size=32768 --output models/tokenizer.json\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Verify the dry-run tokenizer works for training\n",
    "    meta = json.load(open('models/tokenizer_meta.json'))\n",
    "    print(f'Using tokenizer from dry-run (vocab={meta[\"vocab_size\"]})')\n",
    "    print(f'  Compression ratio: {meta[\"compression_ratio\"]}')"
    "    if meta['vocab_size'] < 32768:\n",
    "        print('  NOTE: Using smaller vocab from dry-run. Run full training for 32768 vocab.')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('  Full vocab tokenizer ready.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Verify Local Dry Run ✅\n",
    "\n",
    "Before touching cloud GPU, we verify the training pipeline works on your local RTX 2070:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install dependencies (Colab/Kaggle runtime)\n",
    "!pip install torch transformers datasets 2>&1 | tail -3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clone and set up the repo\n",
    "%cd /content  # Use /kaggle/working on Kaggle\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/ikaaros/nanocore-s1.git 2>/dev/null || git clone https://github.com/KidIkaros/nanocore-s1.git\n",
    "%cd nanocore-s1\n",
    "!pip install -e . 2>/dev/null || true"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run dry-run to verify pipeline works\n",
    "%time python scripts/train_base.py --dry-run"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Full Training on Cloud GPU\n",
    "\n",
    "Once dry-run passes, run full pretraining. Uses FineWeb-EDU (free from HuggingFace).\n",
    "Estimated time: 15-20 min on T4/A10, 8-10 min on T4/V100.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Full Stage 1 training (200M tokens)\n",
    "# batch_size=32, grad_accum=16, effective_batch=512\n",
    "%time python scripts/train_base.py --batch-size=32 --grad-accum=16 --max-steps=1000"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Auto-Commit Results to GitHub\n",
    "\n",
    "Automatically commits the trained checkpoint and report back to GitHub.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Set up git for auto-commit\n",
    "!git config --global user.email \"nanocore@bot.com\"\n",
    "!git config --global user.name \"NanoCore Bot\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use GitHub token for push (set as secret in Colab/Kaggle)\n",
    "import os\n",
    "token = os.environ.get('GH_TOKEN') or os.environ.get('GITHUB_TOKEN')\n",
    "if token:\n",
    "    remote = f'https://{token}@github.com/ikaaros/nanocore-s1.git'\n",
    "    !git remote set-url origin {remote}\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('Set GH_TOKEN env var for auto-push')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Commit and push results\n",
    "import json, os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check the training report\n",
    "if os.path.exists('models/training_report.json'):\n",
    "    with open('models/training_report.json') as f:\n",
    "        report = json.load(f)\n",
    "    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Commit\n",
    "!git add models/nanocore-s1-base.pt models/training_report.json\n",
    "!git commit -m \"train: Stage 1 base model (auto from cloud GPU)\" || true\n",
    "!git push origin main 2>/dev/null || print('No token set - push skipped')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
